  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Veeraiah vs The Commissioner on 21 February, 2023 Author: G.R.Swaminathan Bench: G.R.Swaminathan W.P(Md) Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 21.02.2023 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice G.R.Swaminathan W.P(MD)No.3440 of 2023 and W.M.P.(MD)No.3197, 3198 & 3200 of 2023 M.Veeraiah ... Pet Vs. 1.The Commissioner, Pudukottai Municipality, Pudukottai. 2.The Chairman, Pudukottai Municipality, Pudukottai. ... Resp Prayer : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of In praying this Court to issue a Writ of Certiorari, to call for the record the impugned re-tender notice in Na.Ka.No.5959/2021/A4, dated 13.02.2023 issued by the first respondent and quash the same as illegal.",
    "facts": "2. The petitioner challenges the impugned auction notice dated 13.02.2023 whereby it is proposed to bring 8 shops for auction. The shops are to function as fish vending stalls. 3. The grievance of the petitioner is that he was allotted the shop in the same complex way back in November 2020. He had already remitted a sum of Rs.3,00,000/- as security deposit. However, the shop was not allotted to him. Likewise, the petitioner and few other allottees filed writ petitions before this Court. Vide order dated 15.11.2022 made in W.P.(MD)Nos.22034 to 22037 of 2022, a positive direction was given to the Municipality to open the fish market situated at T.V.S.Corner Fish Market on or before 30.11.2022. 4. I consciously refrain from going into the said allegations. It is for the competent authority concerned to look into the said issue. The petitioner is given liberty to lodge a complaint before the competent authority under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and the said authority is directed to look into the said complaint.",
    "arguments": "The grievance of the petitioner is that this positive direction given by this Court has not been complied with. The petitioner would allege that the fish market was put up as per FSSAI norms. The area earmarked for dumping waste and disposal had now been converted as shops. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 5. 7. At this stage, the learned standing counsel states that the petitioner's monthly license fee was fixed at Rs.6,150/- and that the petitioner has to pay the entire annual license fee upfront. The petitioner's counsel states that the petitioner is ready to remit the amount of Rs.73,800/- at any time. . There is also force in the contention of the petitioner's counsel that the petitioner and others had offered bid for certain amount on the impression that the fish complex will have only 13 shops.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The grievance of the petitioner is that this positive direction given by this Court has not been complied with. The petitioner would allege that the fish market was put up as per FSSAI norms. The area earmarked for dumping waste and disposal had now been converted as shops. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 5. 7. At this stage, the learned standing counsel states that the petitioner's monthly license fee was fixed at Rs.6,150/- and that the petitioner has to pay the entire annual license fee upfront.",
    "respondent_arguments": "The petitioner's counsel states that the petitioner is ready to remit the amount of Rs.73,800/- at any time. . There is also force in the contention of the petitioner's counsel that the petitioner and others had offered bid for certain amount on the impression that the fish complex will have only 13 shops.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
